Lo-res sphere using "hexagonal pixels". Based on an idea by Aexion,
but smoothed out to get a perfect DE.

The original post by Aexion was;

x*=0.6;//scaling.. don't ask.. 
x*=Resolution;
y*=Resolution;
z*=Resolution;
y=floor(y);
//converts (x,z) to (r,q)
const double temp = floor(x + z);
const double r = floor((floor(z - x) + temp) / 3.0);  
const double q = floor((floor(2 * x + 1) + temp) / 3.0) - r;
x = 3.0/2.0 * r;  //turns back, r q to x z 
z = sqrt(3.0) * (q + r/2.0);
x/=Resolution;
y/=Resolution;
z/=Resolution;

Instead of normal floor(), use the function described in LoResIFS,
to have a smoothed pixel look and a continuous DE.
The formula is complex and approximated but looks nice if resolution
is reasonably high.

Luca GN 2016